    "measured_by": "exp.data_authority.verify.census on weiland-wsl; partition independently re-audited by comparing every materialised state byte-for-byte against the official index the manifest claims for it (450/450 identical)",
    "notes": "The D_lib census is content-level, not field-level: every init-map row is opened as real HDF5, its attrs snapshot compared live, and the library collection's init state required to be byte-identical to the official state at orig_init_state_idx. Per task the D_lib occupancy is exactly 5 official inits, so the remaining 45 split 15/30 into query C and test A'."
  },
  "caveats": [
    "The partition is only meaningful together with its seed and the init map: re-running split_init_pools with a different seed produces a different, equally valid partition, and any artifact calibrated on the old one no longer matches.",
    "test_aprime is the precheck A' pool and must never be read by calibration or fitting; query_c is the fit/cal cohort pool and must never be evaluated on. The split manifest is what downstream scripts bind to for that separation."
  ],
